OE 2: Call get_issue with id "OPS-10" to read the full description. The agent confirms the review covers four owners (Harry Harris, David Shea, Linda Castillo, Robert Finley), that Teresa Wood, Aurora Winona, Lisa Smith and Patricia Nguyen were asked to coordinate on their respective properties, and that drafts were due before end of June. Universe today is 2026-07-01, so the deadline has passed.

OE 3: Call list_comments with issueId "OPS-10" to read the comment thread. The agent finds comment_248a843fe7db59e8afaf8d5b6c71c387 (Brooke Phillips, 2026-05-07) assigning Harry Harris and Robert Finley to Lisa and David Shea and Linda Castillo to Patricia, and requesting occupancy rates, outstanding maintenance backlog and make-ready status per owner. This scopes the work to Harris and Finley and excludes the Shea and Castillo packages.

OE 4: Read comment_79dc83838bd65d678c48b5911f942412 (2026-05-17) and comment_179d6b0702be5ca1b0a1e967e1e136e0 (2026-06-10) on the same thread. The first claims Teresa has Robert Finley's review "locked in for the first week of June, 60 minutes in the afternoon" and announces a move to In Progress. The second claims "all four owner meetings are confirmed on the calendar" and announces a move to In Review. The agent should treat both as narration rather than record state, because OPS-10 still reads state_OPS_0 (Backlog) and its updated_at equals its created_at (2026-05-03T22:11:57.112604-05:00), so the issue never moved.

OE 5: Call list_issue_statuses with team "team_001" to enumerate the five available workflow states: state_OPS_0 Backlog, state_OPS_1 Todo, state_OPS_2 In Progress, state_OPS_3 In Review, state_OPS_4 Done. team_001 is the only team in the workspace, so team selection carries no discriminating information.

OE 6: Search Slack using slack_search_channels with query "owner" (or similar) to resolve the owner relations channel. The agent finds C006 with name "#owner-relations". The other seven channels are C001 #maintenance, C002 #leasing, C003 #general, C004 #make-ready, C005 #vendors, C007 #budget-review and C008 #applications. Every channel in this universe has an empty purpose and an empty topic, so channel selection must be driven by name.

OE 7: Read C006 using slack_read_channel with channel_id "C006". The agent finds 43 messages, of which 37 belong to an unrelated mass email campaign and 6 form a 2026-05-28 owner cluster (56e1b950bbfa5ac9b241d7e13587e299, 831d2b6760205432a20487e2664a607e, a6779a055eaf5fb1893d0ed6d92e3b39, 679eac61fae45c2b9c545f4268396c41, 654d7dd532e45ddba60015c69f25b122 and 2687eb8d7cae501ea99b8c8305f12217). Message 831d2b6760205432a20487e2664a607e (Brooke Phillips) asks Lisa for "occupancy numbers, rent collection status, maintenance ticket activity, and make-ready turn progress" for Robert Finley's Mesa Vista May report. A channel-level read shows the parent but not its reply.

OE 8: Call slack_read_thread with channel_id "C006" and message_ts "1780002480.000000" to open the thread under that parent. The agent finds Lisa Smith's own reply a6779a055eaf5fb1893d0ed6d92e3b39 (thread_parent_id 831d2b6760205432a20487e2664a607e, 2026-05-28): "Robert's Mesa Vista portfolio is sitting at 94% occupancy, one unit still in make-ready targeting early June. Collections at 97%, one late payment cleared after first notice. Closed out three tickets this month including a water heater leak, and the turn is on track." This is the spring read the prompt refers to, and 346 of the 580 Slack messages in this universe are thread replies, so it is invisible without a thread read. Note the parent row carries a latest_reply value of 1782860664.000001 that matches no message anywhere in the universe. The reply itself is dated 2026-05-28 on both its ts and its created_at, so the thread must be reached through thread_parent_id rather than by following latest_reply.

