OE 18: Search Airtable using search_records with baseId "appPropertyOps", table "tblMaintenanceTickets" and query "Finley" or "roof" (or similar) to find outstanding maintenance. The agent finds recb4aeaed326f156 (MT-2026-047, fldPriority selHigh, fldCompletionDate empty, so still open): "Top-floor unit at Finley portfolio property showing missing shingles and interior ceiling water staining - roof damage appears to exceed routine patching and requires professional evaluation. Flagged by Lisa Smith for priority assessment and licensed roofing contractor inspection." This is the only open repair ticket in either owner's scope, but it is not the only open ticket: rec46234590708b5c (MT-2026-0184) and recc0ecc885e9645e (DLQ-2026-0601) are both selHigh with an empty fldCompletionDate and both are Tanya Mitchell delinquency records on Sunset Ridge Unit 14, which is Harris's property. Seven rows in the table are open in total. Open status must be read from an empty fldCompletionDate because the table carries no status field, and that empty value is stored two ways, as an empty string and as null.

